<component type="desktop-application">
    <id>app.elysiae.Elysiae</id>
    <name>Elysiae</name>
    <summary>Universal "Anime Game" Launcher</summary>
    <developer id="app.elysiae">
        <name>The Elysiae Project</name>
    </developer>
    <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
    <project_license>BSD-3-Clause</project_license>
    <description>
        <p>
            Elysiae is a universal and performant launcher for "anime games" developed by a certain Chinese video game company.
        </p>
        <p>**Features**</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Safe: Elysiae does not provide mods/plugins or use them to launch games, and the project is ran by the Elysiae Project for free. Elysiae should be safer to use than the alternative launchers</li>
            <li>Low memory usage: ~130MB idle and ~350MB when downloading content</li>
            <li>Low base installation size: We optimized everything in Elysiae to have as little of an impact on your system as possible. </li>
            <li>Faster download speeds: Elysiae uses irmin, our in-house Sophon assembler, to get download speeds as fast as possible for your network</li>
            <li>Runtime: We created Phlogiston, a fork of Proton-GE, to help squeeze out as many frames as possible by optimising exclusively for the games we support</li>
            <li>Maintained: The Elysiae project is committed to maintaining the launcher and fixing issues where possible</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Elysiae is also customisable to fit your preferences. Current options include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>What voice-over language to download</li>
            <li>What language to display on screen (localised lancher text coming soon)</li>
            <li>Weather or not to create a Desktop shortcut on launch</li>
            <li>Toggling auto-updates/pre-install downloads as they become available</li>
        </ul>
    </description>
    <launchable type="desktop-id">app.elysiae.Elysiae.desktop</launchable>
    <provides>
        <id>Elysiae.desktop</id>
    </provides>
